{
  "contract": "intelimensa-identity-v1",
  "description": "Shared fixture for the per-unit identity record and the dcGetIdentity reply (firmware/DEVICE_IDENTITY.md). Owner: firmware repo (testdata/identity-vectors.json); copies elsewhere must be byte-identical (sync-vectors.sh). records: a parser given recordHex (64 bytes, or as noted) must give `expect`; where a record has `build`, a builder given those parts must produce exactly recordHex, and replyHex is what the unit sends for it. `hostsOnly` records are not exactly 64 bytes, so the firmware's parser (which is handed 64) skips them. replies: a host given wireHex must give `expect` (a strict host, one that validates what it reads, must refuse `strictHostsOnly` ones; a host that only shows the serial need not). buildRejects: a builder must refuse these parts. crc32: the record's CRC is zlib's CRC-32, whose check value for '123456789' is cbf43926.",
  "crc32Check": {
    "inputAscii": "123456789",
    "crc32": "cbf43926"
  },
  "codeAlphabet": "0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ",
  "records": [
    {
      "name": "typical",
      "note": "a serial as the server issues it and a registration code",
      "build": {
        "serial": "MSV3G01SATKX",
        "code": "7KQ49XT2AM"
      },
      "recordHex": "4449534d010c0a004d5356334730315341544b580000000000000000000000000000000000000000374b513439585432414d00000000000000000000b15ebe03",
      "replyHex": "000c4d5356334730315341544b580a374b513439585432414d",
      "expect": {
        "valid": true,
        "serial": "MSV3G01SATKX",
        "code": "7KQ49XT2AM"
      }
    },
    {
